To add a sticky footer or header to a webpage using CSS, follow these steps:

1. First, create an HTML element for the header or footer. You can use the <header> or <footer> tags for this purpose.

2. Define the width, height, and position of the header or footer using CSS. For instance, you can set the width to 100% to ensure that the header or footer spans the entire width of the webpage. You can also set the height according to your requirements, such as 50px for a small header or footer.

3. To make the header or footer fixed, use the position property in CSS. Set it to "fixed" and specify the top or bottom position. For instance, to make the header fixed at the top of the page, use the following code: 

    header {
        position: fixed;
        top: 0;
        width: 100%;
        height: 50px;
    }

4. To prevent the content below the header or footer from getting covered up, add padding to the main content area. The padding should match the height of the header or footer. For example, if your header is 50px tall, add this code to the main content area:

    main {
        padding-top: 50px;
    }

5. For the footer, you can use a similar approach but set the position property to "fixed" and the bottom position. Remember to add padding to the bottom of the main content area.

    footer {
        position: fixed;
        bottom: 0;
        width: 100%;
        height: 50px;
    }

    main {
        padding-bottom: 50px;
    }

